zeroWidthT -- A ZERO-WIDTH LEAF ON THE NEW ROAD (SEQ 208-209, 2026-09-27).

A max > 1 LEAF with min 0 -- nameSet* in NamE, Modifier* in TraiT and TraiTdata -- never enters
parseLoop, so before SEQ 209 nothing owned its zero-width match: exitFromParse's min-zero tail was
guarded max <= 1 and answered 0. The fix asks repeatsInLoop and lets a leaf succeed on zero width.

BlocK { x = 1; } is the nameSet case: a one-letter name leaves nameSet nothing to match. It is driven
at TOP LEVEL because a drive from inside an action refuses -- parseRule's enclosing-rule lookup finds
the action's own cached body, which is also tagged BlocK. Read off the drive's 2b-before-pop mark:
the remaining input, which must be the end of input.
TraiT abc / TraiT abc+?! are the Modifier* case, zero modifiers and several, both roads.
Generated with parser(DO), as sweepT does.
